# Matt Petiteau

I'm a Senior Software Engineer based in London. Ten years building backend
systems that have to keep running: order and inventory platforms, software
driving a 24/7 prescription factory, security scanning pipelines, and the
platform and ground robotics behind the NHS drone delivery network. Mostly in
start-ups and fast paced teams, so I've owned the whole lifecycle, from spec and
design through to the infrastructure it runs on, and whatever breaks at 3am. These days I spend as
much time on architecture, design review and mentoring as on writing code
myself.

## Experience

[Senior Backend Engineer at [Apian](https://apian.health)]{.title}
[Aug 2023 to present]{.date}\
Architect the platform behind the NHS drone delivery network, and lead the
robotics stack for autonomous in-hospital deliveries.

[Senior Software Engineer at [Skin + Me](https://www.skinandme.com)]{.title}
[Sept 2021 to Aug 2023]{.date}\
Built factory management systems running a bespoke 24/7 facility producing
thousands of personalised prescription orders a day.

[Software Engineer at [Bramfitt Tech Labs](https://bramfitt-tech-labs.com)]{.title}
[Feb 2020 to Sept 2021]{.date}\
Built a vulnerability management platform automating security scanning for a
major energy company, designed hand in hand with pentesters and security
experts.

[Freelance Software Engineer]{.title}
[2019 to 2020]{.date}\
Web applications, integrations and backend systems for early-stage e-commerce
start-ups.

[Lead Developer at Soda Says]{.title}
[Oct 2018 to Dec 2019]{.date}\
First technical hire, automated stock and order management end to end, letting
a very small team run at a scale that would otherwise have needed a third party
warehouse team.

[Software Engineer at [Eve Sleep](https://www.evesleep.co.uk)]{.title}
[Sept 2017 to Oct 2018]{.date}\
Dedicated engineer to operations, building tooling and automation for
logistics, inventory and orders. Brought in by a former manager from Made.com,
who hired me again a year later at Soda Says.

[Operations, EU at [Made.com](https://www.made.com)]{.title}
[Jan 2016 to Sept 2017]{.date}\
Automated my own role and several processes. Moved into engineering full time
after that.

[Supply Chain Engineer at [Kuhn Group](https://www.kuhn.com)]{.title}
[Sept 2013 to Aug 2015]{.date}\
Excel wizard, and lots of VBA.

## Skills

Python, SQL, Bash, Go, JS, Elisp. REST APIs, microservices, message queues,
event-driven pipelines. PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, Redis, MongoDB. GCP, AWS,
Azure, Terraform, Docker, Linux, CI/CD. ROS 2, Nav2, SLAM. SAST,
DAST and SCA. System architecture, design review, mentoring, and a fair bit of
soldering.

## Projects

A few things I've built across widely different domains, hardware, security,
fonts and embedded.

[Smallcat](https://github.com/smallwat3r/smallcat), 26-key split
keyboard, designed end to end, and the one I type on every day.\
[Shhh](https://github.com/smallwat3r/shhh), encrypted one-time secret sharing,
in Flask.\
[Secretapi](https://github.com/smallwat3r/secretapi), the successor to Shhh,
rewritten in Go with a CLI client.\
[Rpi-gardener](https://github.com/smallwat3r/rpi-gardener), houseplant
monitoring on a Raspberry Pi and a Pico.\
[Ocrab](https://github.com/smallwat3r/ocrab-font), a monospace font merging
OCR A and OCR B, with a few tweaks. Two typefaces designed for optical
character recognition, so no character can be mistaken for another.

More of them on [github](https://github.com/smallwat3r), or written up on this
blog.

